About the Company &nbsp;

At Torc, we have always believed that autonomous vehicle technology will transform how we travel, move freight, and do business. &nbsp;
A leader in autonomous driving since 2007, Torc has spent over a decade commercializing our solutions with experienced partners.  Now a part of the Daimler family , we are focused solely on developing software for automated trucks to transform how the world moves freight. &nbsp;
Join us and catapult your career with the company that helped pioneer autonomous technology, and the first AV software company with the vision to partner directly with a truck manufacturer. &nbsp;

Meet the Team &nbsp;

The Senior Autonomy Core Frameworks Software Engineer plays a critical role in architecting and advancing the foundational frameworks that underpin Torc's autonomous driving stack. This role helps in owning technical direction for the software in core autonomy components, helping to raise the bar on code quality, and driving improvements across the autonomy software. &nbsp;

As a senior technical leader, you will collaborate closely with the Behavior and Perception teams within Autonomy to design robust, composable architectural patterns that serve as the foundation for safe, performant, reliable autonomous operation. This position demands deep technical expertise in software architecture and autonomous vehicle fundamentals. &nbsp;

What You’ll Do &nbsp;

• Lead the architecture, design, implementation, and evolution of core frameworks that serve as the foundation for Torc's autonomous driving stack, including state management, inter- component communication, abstraction layers, and common utilities used across all software systems.

• Drive&nbsp; the technical direction for real-time C++ architectural components and patterns responsible for reliable system-wide data flow, component coordination, error handling, and operational observability.

• Establish scalable architectural patterns and abstractions that enable autonomous driving capabilities while driving technical tradeoff discussions and long-term design decisions that shape the entire platform.

• Collaborate across Behavior and Perception teams to keep integration boundaries clean and shared abstractions coherent.

• Lead architecture reviews, design discussions, and code reviews while&nbsp; establishing engineering standards that improve reliability, maintainability, testability, and scalability across the platform.

• Mentor software engineers through technical coaching, architectural guidance, and day-to-day collaboration while raising engineering standards and fostering technical excellence across the organization.

• Champion architectural quality through systematic validation, comprehensive testing strategies, observability frameworks, and production readiness practices that ensure platform robustness at scale.

• Contribute to&nbsp; root cause analysis of complex platform-level issues and drive architectural improvements that enhance system reliability, performance, and operational resilience.

• Define and evolve simulation and validation frameworks that enable rigorous testing of core architectural components across diverse operational scenarios and edge cases.

• Evaluate emerging architectural patterns,&nbsp; systems research, and advanced techniques that can strengthen the platform's foundation and enable future autonomous driving capabilities.

• Communicate complex architectural concepts and technical vision effectively across engineering teams, product, and leadership while building consensus around platf orm direction and technical strategy. &nbsp;

What You’ll Need to Succeed &nbsp;

• Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Robotics, Electrical Engineering, or related technical discipline with 8+ years of professional software engineering experience, or

• Master's degree with 6+ years of professional experience, or

• Demonstrated success designing and evolving complex, production software platforms w

We are a global team of innovators and pioneers dedicated to shaping the future of observability. At New Relic, we build an intelligent platform that empowers companies to thrive in an AI-first world by giving them unparalleled insight into their complex systems. As we continue to expand our global footprint, we're looking for passionate people to join our mission. If you're ready to help the world's best companies optimize their digital applications, we invite you to explore a career with us!

Your opportunity

At New Relic, we believe in a virtuous cycle where customer success fuels improved revenue performance . Our Account Manager role is a pivotal function of an updated pod structure that sits at the intersection of Customer Success, Sales, and Product. Focused squarely on securing and growing our existing revenue base. We are a passionate, upbeat, and highly motivated group committed to exceptional customer loyalty, support, and expansion.&nbsp;

We are seeking an Account Manager to join our team and make a positive impact in the continued success and growth of our organization. In this critical role, you will be a driver of retention, adoption, and expansion. Strong leadership ensures positive relationships and alignment across Product, Marketing, and Sales, and Support. If you are passionate about building deep, strategic customer relationships and thrive in a quota-carrying environment, let's talk!

&nbsp;

What you'll do

You will utilize your skills in customer success, renewals, and sales methodologies to exceed customer expectations and deliver value across multiple key performance indicators.&nbsp;

Drive Revenue &amp; Retention &nbsp;

• Pod Collaboration: In partnership with the Account Team, you will function as a secondary seller within a unified pod structure. This role is essential in supporting the Account Executive (Core Seller) through seamless cross-functional alignment and collaborative deal execution. You will review areas of opportunity (whitespace analysis), organize and manage enablement sessions with Technical Success Managers, and in partnership with the Solutions Consultants, help drive new growth opportunities for Account Executives.&nbsp;

• Secure &amp; Negotiate Renewals: Build positive relationships with customers including economic buyers, decision-makers, champions and end-users, negotiating contracts for direct and partner managed agreements.&nbsp;

• Mitigate Churn: Proactively identify accounts running "cold" and/or at risk (downgrades, churn, low BCM Burn Rate) and develop strategic plans to mitigate uncertainty, drive customer satisfaction, increase consumption, and maintain high renewal rates.&nbsp;

• Deliver Expansion: Grow revenue at renewal time and throughout the customer lifecycle. Increase Billable Consumption Metric (BCM) for current subscription customers and convert Pay-As-You-Go (PAYG) customers through sub-account prospecting and finding new upsell opportunities.&nbsp;

Cultivate Customer Success &amp; Adoption &nbsp;

• Improve Customer Relationships: Collaborate with Account Executives on accounts at key moments in the customer journey, becoming their voice within New Relic.

• Coordinate Customer Business Reviews

• Contribute to Account Plans

• Complete the Renewal Process &amp; Discussions&nbsp;

• Increase Adoption: Support customer Onboarding and strengthen product knowledge through:

• Account Health Checks&nbsp;

• Business Value Assessments Enablement Sessions&nbsp;

• Advocate &amp; Resolve: Collaborate with departments (Sales, Operations, Customer Solutions, Legal, and Collections) to resolve customer issues and advocate on their behalf.&nbsp;

Strategic Execution &amp; Data Analysis &nbsp;

• Value Articulation: Effectively communicate company messages and our value proposition, both verbally and in writing.&nbsp;

• Data-Driven Strategy: Use strong analytical skills and experience working with data to professionally advise strategy, identify industry trend

O que buscamos:
Apoiar o desenvolvimento, manutenção e evolução de aplicações na plataforma ServiceNow, colaborando com equipes de negócio, analistas funcionais, arquitetos e desenvolvedores.
Requisitos e qualificações;

• Desenvolver e manter aplicações na plataforma ServiceNow utilizando boas práticas;

• Apoiar a configuração e customização de módulos como App Engine, Customer Service Management (CSM) e ITSM;

• Criar e manter Client Scripts, Business Rules, Script Includes, UI Policies, Flow Designer e Record Producers;

• Participar da análise técnica de requisitos funcionais e não funcionais;

• Apoiar a integração da plataforma ServiceNow com sistemas internos e externos por meio de APIs REST e SOAP;

• Participar das cerimônias ágeis do time e colaborar com a evolução contínua dos processos;

• Manter as atividades atualizadas no Jira;

• Buscar constante capacitação técnica na plataforma ServiceNow e tecnologias relacionadas;

•
Requisitos e Qualificações :

• Conhecimento básico em desenvolvimento JavaScript;

• Conhecimento ou experiência em módulos App Engine, ITSM ou CSM;

• Conhecimento da plataforma ServiceNow;

• Conhecimento básico em APIs REST e SOAP;

• Conhecimento básico em banco de dados e modelagem de dados;

• Familiaridade com conceitos de desenvolvimento web;

• Conhecimento de metodologias ágeis como Scrum ou Kanban;

• Capacidade de aprendizado contínuo e interesse em desenvolvimento de soluções corporativas;

• Boa comunicação e habilidade para trabalho em equipe;

•
Diferenciais :

• Conhecimento em Flow Designer e Service Portal;

• Conhecimento básico em integrações por microsserviços;

Descrição comportamental:
Procuramos uma pessoa que:

• Goste de trabalhar em equipe e seja colaborativa em suas atribuições;

• Tenha coragem para se desafiar e ir além, abraçando novas oportunidades de crescimento;

• Transforme ideias em soluções criativas e busque qualidade em toda sua rotina;

• Tenha habilidades de resolução de problemas ;

• Possua habilidade e se sinta confortável para trabalhar de forma independente e gerenciar o próprio tempo ;

• Tenha interesse em lidar com situações adversas e inovadoras no âmbito tecnológico.

